//? Title: Salsa20/20: actual ARX rounds, official core vector and stream blocks
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Turn a key, nonce and counter into a byte stream, then XOR it with a message.
Actual quarter-round records connect addition, rotation and XOR to the official
core vector before the original message round trip.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Each quarter round updates four 32-bit words with addition modulo 2^32, XOR and
rotations 7,9,13,18. Ten column/row double rounds are followed by addition of
the original sixteen-word state and little-endian serialization. For block j,
use counter+j; C_i=P_i XOR K_i, so applying the same stream twice recovers P.
This identity proves round-trip behavior, not security. The original plaintext
contains fewer than 64 bytes despite its wording; its actual block count is
measured below. A separate 145-byte binary control exercises three blocks. This
API is the bare cipher, with no authentication or message-format protocol.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/salsa20_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/salsa20.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto e = a::salsa20_example();
    auto r = a::salsa20_core_trace(e.input);
    const auto &q = r.quarters[0];
    std::print("Actual first quartet indices `{}`; before `{}`; after `{}`.\nActual core vector agrees with " "all 64 official bytes: {}.\n",
               q.indices, q.before, q.after, r.bytes == e.expected);
    if (r.bytes != e.expected)
        return 1;
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "16 little-endian input words");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual quarter rounds {}",
                                     r.quarters.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Official 64-byte agreement {}",
                                     r.bytes == e.expected));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/salsa20_tiny.svg");
}
```
